1.  A room cannot have two reservations for the same day.

To enforce this constraint, we create a BEFORE INSERT trigger that checks for overlapping reservations.

✅ Solution: Using a Trigger
------------------------------------------

CREATE TRIGGER trg_CheckRoomAvailability
ON RoomReservation
FOR INSERT
AS
BEGIN
    IF EXISTS (
        SELECT 1
        FROM RoomReservation r
        JOIN inserted i ON r.HotelID = i.HotelID 
                      AND r.RoomID = i.RoomID
                      AND i.FromDate < r.ToDate 
                      AND i.ToDate > r.FromDate
    )
    BEGIN
        RAISERROR ('A room cannot have two reservations for the same day.', 16, 1);
        ROLLBACK TRANSACTION;
    END
END;



------------------------------------------


CREATE TRIGGER trg_CheckRoomAvailability → Defines a new trigger named trg_CheckRoomAvailability.
ON RoomReservation → This trigger is associated with the RoomReservation table.
FOR INSERT → The trigger fires after an INSERT operation (i.e., when a new reservation is being added).




AS → Specifies the body of the trigger.
BEGIN → Marks the start of the trigger logic.


IF EXISTS (...) → Checks if there is an overlapping reservation.
SELECT 1 → A simple way to check for conflicts (returns 1 if a conflict exists).
FROM RoomReservation r → Alias r represents existing reservations.
JOIN inserted i → inserted is a special table in SQL Server that stores the new row(s) being inserted.
ON r.HotelID = i.HotelID AND r.RoomID = i.RoomID → Ensures we are checking reservations for the same hotel and same room.
AND i.FromDate < r.ToDate AND i.ToDate > r.FromDate → Checks for date overlap:
i.FromDate < r.ToDate → The new reservation starts before an existing reservation ends.
i.ToDate > r.FromDate → The new reservation ends after an existing reservation starts.
These two conditions ensure that even partial overlaps are caught.


BEGIN ... END → Executes the error handling block only if a conflict is found.
RAISERROR ('A room cannot have two reservations for the same day.', 16, 1);
RAISERROR generates a custom error message.
'A room cannot have two reservations for the same day.' → Error message displayed to the user.
16 → Error severity level (16 = user-defined error).
1 → State number (used to track errors internally).
ROLLBACK TRANSACTION; → Cancels the insertion if a conflict is detected, preventing double booking.


Marks the end of the trigger logic.


Final Explanation:
This trigger ensures no two reservations overlap for the same hotel room. Whenever a new reservation is added:

It checks for conflicts by joining the RoomReservation table with the inserted table.
If an overlap is found, it raises an error and cancels the transaction.
If no conflicts exist, the new reservation is successfully inserted.
This approach maintains data integrity and ensures rooms are not double-booked. 🚀


