1. For each city, give the currently most expensive hotel in its historical center.
💡 Explanation:
"Currently" means checking the price where ToDate IS NULL in HotelRoomPrice.
"Most expensive" is based on the maximum room price.
The hotel must be inside the historic center (ST_Within).


-------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------

SELECT c.CityID, c.Name AS CityName, h.HotelID, h.HotelName, MAX(p.PricePerNight) AS MaxPrice
FROM City c
JOIN Hotel h ON h.CityID = c.CityID
JOIN HotelRoom hr ON hr.HotelID = h.HotelID
JOIN HotelRoomPrice p ON p.HotelID = hr.HotelID AND p.RoomID = hr.RoomID
WHERE ST_Within(h.HotelGeo, c.HistoricCenterGeo)
  AND p.ToDate IS NULL
GROUP BY c.CityID, c.Name, h.HotelID, h.HotelName;

